        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "71fc7a4d-3170-5f51-859e-1adf16e2ae98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manchester, New Hampshire, northern New England\n- Buildings: Brady Sullivan Plaza, Hampshire Plaza, One City Hall Plaza, City Hall Plaza, City Hall Plaza Tower, 900 Elm Street\n- Addresses: 1000 Elm Street, 900 Elm Street\n\nFacts:\n- Brady Sullivan Plaza, formerly known as Hampshire Plaza, was completed in 1972 as a 259-foot, 20-story high-rise at 1000 Elm Street in Manchester, New Hampshire.\n- From 1972 until 1992, Brady Sullivan Plaza was the tallest building in New Hampshire and northern New England.\n- In 1992, the completion of One City Hall Plaza at 900 Elm Street ended Brady Sullivan Plaza’s status as the tallest building in New Hampshire and northern New England.\n- City Hall Plaza, also called City Hall Plaza Tower or 900 Elm Street, is a 275-foot office tower in Manchester, New Hampshire.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
